  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city of Venice is built on more than 100 small islands in the marshy lagoon along the Adriatic Sea. Its unique position has made it a centre for trade and commerce since ancient times, attracting merchants from all over Europe. The Rialto Bridge, which spans the Grand Canal, was originally a wooden bridge but was rebuilt in stone in the early 16th century by Antonio da Ponte. Today, the bridge is one of the most famous landmarks in Venice, drawing millions of tourists each year.\n\nVenice's economy has traditionally been based on shipbuilding and trade, with its skilled craftsmen producing beautiful gondolas and other boats. However, with the decline of the Venetian Empire in the 18th century, the city's fortunes began to change. Many of its inhabitants moved away, seeking better opportunities elsewhere.\n\nDespite these challenges, Venice has managed to reinvent itself as a major tourist destination. The city's rich history and cultural heritage have been preserved and showcased through various museums, galleries, and festivals. Visitors can explore the stunning St Mark's Basilica, admire the intricate mosaics in the Doge's Palace, or take a romantic gondola ride along the canals.\n\nHowever, this influx of tourists has also brought about some negative consequences. The city is struggling to cope with the sheer number of visitors, leading to overcrowding and pollution. Some critics argue that Venice's unique character is being lost in the process, as it becomes increasingly commercialized and touristy.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason why tourists visit Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To admire its beautiful beaches\", \"To experience its rich cultural heritage\", \"To enjoy its vibrant nightlife\", \"To attend its famous music festivals\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To experience its rich cultural heritage\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the passage, what was the original material used for the Rialto Bridge?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Wood\", \"Stone\", \"Metal\", \"Glass\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Wood\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards the commercialization of Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Positive\", \"Negative\", \"Neutral\", \"Indifferent\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Negative\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What has been a major challenge for Venice in recent times?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Overpopulation\", \"Pollution\", \"Economic decline\", \"All of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"All of the above\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"Why did many Venetians leave the city in the 18th century?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To escape the crowded streets\", \"To seek better economic opportunities elsewhere\", \"To avoid the pollution\", \"To attend the festivals\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To seek better economic opportunities elsewhere\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
